{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"190","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"C. STL"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya used to be an accountant before the war began and he is one of the few who knows how to operate a computer, so he was assigned as the programmer."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"We all know that programs often store sets of integers. For example, if we have a problem about a weighted directed graph, its edge can be represented by three integers: the number of the starting vertex, the number of the final vertex and the edge's weight. So, as Vasya was trying to represent characteristics of a recently invented robot in his program, he faced the following problem."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Vasya is not a programmer, so he asked his friend Gena, what the convenient way to store "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers is. Gena used to code in language X-"},{"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"- and so he can use only the types that occur in this language. Let's define, what a \"type\" is in language X-"},{"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"-:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" First, a type is a string \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"int"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\". "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Second, a type is a string that starts with \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pair"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\", then followed by angle brackets listing "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly two"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" comma-separated other types of language X-"},{"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"-. This record contains no spaces. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" No other strings can be regarded as types. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"More formally: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"type"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" := "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"int"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" | "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pair<type,type>"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". For example, Gena uses the following type for graph edges: "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pair<int,pair<int,int>"},{"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Gena was pleased to help Vasya, he dictated to Vasya a type of language X-"},{"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"-, that stores "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers. Unfortunately, Gena was in a hurry, so he omitted the punctuation. Now Gena has already left and Vasya can't find the correct punctuation, resulting in a type of language X-"},{"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"-, however hard he tries."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Help Vasya and add the punctuation marks so as to receive the valid type of language X-"},{"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"-. Otherwise say that the task is impossible to perform."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"(1 ≤ n ≤ 105)"},{"kind":"text","text":", showing how many numbers the type dictated by Gena contains."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains space-separated words, said by Gena. Each of them is either \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"pair"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" or \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"int"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the total number of words does not exceed "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"105"},{"kind":"text","text":" and that among all the words that Gena said, there are exactly "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" words \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"int"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If it is possible to add the punctuation marks so as to get a correct type of language X-"},{"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"- as a result, print a single line that represents the resulting type. Otherwise, print \""},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Error occurred"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"\" (without the quotes). "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Inside the record of a type should not be any extra spaces and other characters"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that if such type exists, then it is unique."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that you should print the type dictated by Gena (if such type exists) and not any type that can contain "},{"kind":"math_inline","text":"n"},{"kind":"text","text":" values."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\npair pair int int int\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"pair<pair<int,int>,int>"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\npair int\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"Error occurred"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"C","problemCode":"190C","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/190/problem/C"}